   "statement": "At 4 N m the friction capacity at the minimum preload with a cold joint (6.00 kN) is below the LC1 joint load (6.44 kN): at the low end of the scatter the head can slip into bearing at the first pressurisation of a normal firing (at 5.53 N m it held, 8.29 kN). LC2 and FA1S were bearing-type at any torque (234 (1)(c)). Once in bearing the screws are shear pins at LC1 too: case bearing 41.2 MPa per screw at LC1 (unfactored) against Fbry 324 MPa (78.6 C), so hole damage per firing is not expected; the slip (up to the 0.26 mm radial hole clearance, match-drilled) is a one-way settle to bearing, then a small cyclic bearing load each firing: fretting and wear are covered by the gauge interval. Loosening: the thread locker, not the preload, retains the screw (M-T1L); the bore O-rings g1/g2 are radial seals and do not depend on the axial position within the hole clearance (FEA3D's 231 (3) contact sub-model with preload at nominal and +25 % confirms the slip and bearing)"
